                <pb facs="0991" n="983" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg983"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1261: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Beirut</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Palmer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-09T19:00:00-05:00">November 9, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of November 8, 3 p.m. If you have not already done so, it is
                    suggested that you acknowledge the communications addressed to you concerning
                    Palestine and furnish such correspondents with the Department’s public statement
                    on the subject contained in radio bulletin No. 241 of October 14, 1938. You may
                    add that the statement represents no change in this Government’s position in the
                    matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
